{"title":"2016 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Graph_for_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Graph for Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Elijahman\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Elijahman</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Education,_The_Study_of_Everything\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Education, The Study of Everything</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Omega_Learn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Omega Learn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two congruent circles centered at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> each pass through the other circle's center. The line containing both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is extended to intersect the circles at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. The circles intersect at two points, one of which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. What is the degree measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e8dd80cb1927f03ef77da74c59e77acf710c815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CED$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22cd69b203c6c24cfd48aad4ad34fb33642c26c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }90\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }105\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }120\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }135\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"434\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf736a0eb0e4f959e57e0dc8ac818f51350a1192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EAB}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral (all are radii of congruent circles). Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/7/27704de92a30a27c541dc8969cc6a1a3fc8aeded.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle{AEB}=m\\angle{EAB}=m\\angle{EBA} = 60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"311\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is a straight line, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75ec5a1917eaebbc195ac9e01bc576f9bb28275e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle{EBD} = 180^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}=120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"238\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb3ba511c5aae6aff5bc372439d3d9a1de372b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=BD$\" width=\"83\" height=\"12\" /> (both are radii of the same circle), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/1/6c10f38f3a034c71a2153e7736b073786fa18ba7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{BED}$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/d/85ddc71d4926fb6c3ef57565f2f71113a02fcd3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle{BED}=m\\angle{BDE}=30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"219\" height=\"13\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1ed9665b688481d9898cae674d430262a5b2c9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle{AEC}=m\\angle{ACE}=30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"219\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/5984463c4932a07e8837871c5ba96a13671dd172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CED}=m\\angle{AEC}+m\\angle{AEB}+m\\angle{BED} = 30^{\\circ}+60^{\\circ}+30^{\\circ} = 120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"545\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2ad77203ffe63dbf8edc051f3f5ea36c8f38c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\ 120}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"81\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Graph_for_Solution_1\">Graph for Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Graph for Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sNkKxIi7_SpxihTp0QrOcD3Js14buvd8/view?usp=drivesdk\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sNkKxIi7_SpxihTp0QrOcD3Js14buvd8/view?usp=drivesdk</a>\n~ By Quetzalcoatlus\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Elijahman\">Video Solution by Elijahman</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Elijahman\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UZqVG5Q1liA?si=LDc8tMTnj1FMMlZc\">https://youtu.be/UZqVG5Q1liA?si=LDc8tMTnj1FMMlZc</a>\n</p><p>~Elijahman\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Education.2C_The_Study_of_Everything\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Education,_The_Study_of_Everything\">Video Solution by Education, The Study of Everything</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Education, The Study of Everything\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/iGG_Hz-V6lU\">https://youtu.be/iGG_Hz-V6lU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Omega_Learn\">Video Solution by Omega Learn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Omega Learn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FDgcLW4frg8?t=968\">https://youtu.be/FDgcLW4frg8?t=968</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nLlnMO6D5ek\">https://youtu.be/nLlnMO6D5ek</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 8\">2016 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2016\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Problems/Problem